Subject: [PATCH] tofi: clean up keyboard keymap mapping once

The non-late keyboard path unmapped and closed the keymap fd before updating
the xkb state, then fell through to the shared cleanup and did the same work a
second time. Darwin/iOS terminates the process with EXC_GUARD DEALLOC_GAP on
that second munmap.

Keep the common cleanup at the end of the callback and let both paths share it.
---
 src/main.c | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/main.c b/src/main.c
index 3c2bc4d..a23b24c 100644
--- a/src/main.c
+++ b/src/main.c
@@ -154,8 +154,6 @@ static void wl_keyboard_keymap(
 				map_shm,
 				XKB_KEYMAP_FORMAT_TEXT_V1,
 				XKB_KEYMAP_COMPILE_NO_FLAGS);
-		munmap(map_shm, size);
-		close(fd);
 
 		struct xkb_state *xkb_state = xkb_state_new(xkb_keymap);
 		xkb_keymap_unref(tofi->xkb_keymap);
